# The attack set — staff-written assessment material. This repo is public, so
# committing it would hand the set to anyone who finds the repo, including
# students who haven't run it. The folder stays on disk; what gets committed
# is results/, which is the part that's graded. Remove these two lines if the
# TF wants the set tracked.
attack_set/
